// Language section: Expressions.
page expressions { sites = [:reference, :wcl_skill]  title = "Expressions"
  h1 "Expressions"

  p "Every field value, function argument, and `let` right-hand side is an **expression** — something that produces a value. WCL's expression grammar is small: literals, identifiers, member access, calls, operators, and a handful of constructor forms."

  callout "Covered elsewhere" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "Literal forms live with their types (Numbers, Strings, Booleans, Symbols, Optionals, Lists, Tensors). Function literals are in Functions. if / match / let / block expressions are in Control Flow. This chapter focuses on the connective tissue."
  }

  h2 "Operators"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Group"      | "Operators" |
      | "Arithmetic" | "`+` `-` `*` `/` `%`" |
      | "Comparison" | "`==` `!=` `<` `<=` `>` `>=`" |
      | "Logical"    | "`&&` `||` `!`" |
      | "Unary"      | "`-expr` (negate), `!expr` (not)" |
  }

  p "Precedence follows the usual conventions: unary tightest, then `*` `/` `%`, then `+` `-`, then comparison, then `&&`, then `||`. Use parentheses to group when in doubt."

  h2 "Numeric promotion"

  p "Arithmetic and comparison widen mixed numeric operands to a common type, so cross-width and integer/float mixing work without explicit casts."
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
a = 1 + 2.0        // i64 widened to f64 → 3.0
b = 1u32 == 1i64   // true
c = 3.0 * 2u8      // 6.0
WCL
  }

  h2 "Member access"

  p "A dotted path reads a field. Access chains through records, variant payloads, and any composite that exposes named members."
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
region = service.metadata.region
deep   = config.services.web.metadata.region
WCL
  }

  h2 "Function calls"

  p "Parentheses call a function or constructor. Arguments are expressions, evaluated lazily; the call evaluates the body in a fresh context."
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
n      = len(items)
total  = sum(map(items, fn(x: i64) -> i64 x * 2))
shape  = Point { x: 1.0, y: 2.0 }
WCL
  }

  h2 "Variant construction"

  p "Build a union variant with `Union::Variant`. Record bodies go in braces, typeref payloads in parentheses, unit constructors stand bare."
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
a = Shape::Circle { radius: 5.0, stroke: 0.5 }
b = Shape::Polygon(7)
c = Shape::Empty
WCL
  }
  p "See [Unions](unions) for declaring the surrounding variant set."

  h2 "List literals"

  p "Square brackets and commas build a `list<T>`. See [Lists](lists) for nested lists and the collection builtins."
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
xs    = [1, 2, 3]
names = ["alice", "bob"]
empty = []
WCL
  }
}
